Why JWT comes over spring-security ?
Spring Security:
- from filter, request is delegate to AuthenticationManager for Authenticate.
- each and every requests, you need to provide the  login credential (user/pass) which is very hectic and tidious. to over come this JWT has introduce.

Complete Spring-Security Lifecycle
LOGIN REQUEST
     ↓
Security Filter Chain
     ↓
AuthenticationManager
     ↓
AuthenticationProvider
     ↓
UserDetailsService
     ↓
Database
     ↓
Authentication Success
     ↓
SecurityContextHolder
     ↓
Authorization
     ↓
Session (if session-based)
     ↓
Controller
     ↓
Response

JWT:
- At first time ask the user credential(user/pass) and create the token, then for next time they just pass the token and they are able to access the end-point.

How JWT token has generated?
Decoded:
Header - It contains algorithm and token type
Payload - It contains user-name, expiration of token
Verify Signature - It contains secret and validate header/payload/secret, by using those properties it generate the token.
Note: each Header/Payload/Verify Signature having own color to differentiate it
      All components (Header/Payload/Verify Signature) called as claim in JWT

Work flow of spring-security and jwt
1. first invoke the endpoint from controller
2. check the token from request header
3. extract the header token and get the username/token expiration time..., and validate these details(username/token-exp-time) from UserDetails(inbuild class of spring-security) and DB
4. once validation succeeded then endpoint get the access.
Note: JWT work on top of spring-security.

Complete JWT Request Lifecycle
LOGIN
=====
Request
 ↓
Filter
 ↓
AuthenticationManager
 ↓
AuthenticationProvider
 ↓
UserDetailsService
 ↓
DB
 ↓
JWT Generated
 ↓
Client Stores Token


API CALL
========
Request + JWT
 ↓
Security Filter Chain
 ↓
JWT Filter
 ↓
Validate Token(extract the JWT and validate)
 ↓
SecurityContextHolder
 ↓
Controller
 ↓
Response

How to insert the user credential in DB
url: POST http://localhost:8080/products/new
payload: {
             "name": "kumar",
             "password": "pwd1",
             "email": "jone@example.com",
             "roles": "ROLE_ADMIN"

         }

How to generate the token
url: POST http://localhost:8080/products/authenticate
payload: {
             "username": "kumar",
             "password": "pwd1"
         }

How to test endpoints
attached the USER/ADMIN token in header
url: GET http://localhost:8080/products/all, http://localhost:8080/products/12


